+# Optional Mold extension for MatPL LAMMPS
+
+Origin: https://github.com/AndresRTejedor/Mold
+Commit: 6fc7218ad5be70e95bce905ac3819cf513ba4c50
+Installation: https://andresrtejedor.github.io/Mold/install.html
+
+`upstream/` preserves the four official source files and LICENSE verbatim.
+`manifest.json` records their original byte hashes. Copy the four cpp/h files
+to the MatPL-patched LAMMPS src directory, then apply the local patch with:
+
+```sh
+cp extensions/mold/upstream/pair_square_well.{cpp,h} "$LAMMPS_SRC/src/"
+cp extensions/mold/upstream/pair_lj_BG.{cpp,h} "$LAMMPS_SRC/src/"
+patch --binary -d "$LAMMPS_SRC" -p1 < extensions/mold/mold-flat-virial.patch
+```
+
+The official square/well compute() leaves fpair uninitialized in the flat
+well region. This can also reuse a preceding pair's force in ev_tally.
+The patch sets fpair to zero for each pair before selecting the flat or
+transition branch, correcting pair/per-atom virial without changing the
+potential or force formula. The analytic regression fails on the original
+binary (5/33) and passes on the patched one. With MatPL NEP, hybrid uses
+explicit substyle virial, so the correction matters for NPT pressure.
+
+The source retains its original CRLF line endings; --binary preserves them
+while applying the patch. Re-running patch on an already patched tree is
+not required. Reconfigure CMake after installing new sources. No PKG_MOLD
+switch exists; root src files and PairStyle declarations are discovered by
+LAMMPS CMake. See docs/MOLD_CMAKE_GUIDE.md for complete commands and results.
diff --git a/extensions/mold/mold-flat-virial.patch b/extensions/mold/mold-flat-virial.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6d85c11
--- /dev/null
+++ b/extensions/mold/mold-flat-virial.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+--- a/src/pair_square_well.cpp
++++ b/src/pair_square_well.cpp
+@@ -111,6 +111,9 @@
+       jtype = type[j];
+ 
+       if (rsq < cutsq[itype][jtype]) {
++
++        // The flat part of the well has zero force and zero virial.
++        fpair = 0.0;
+ 
+         r2min = (z0[itype][jtype] - 10 * dwell[itype][jtype]);
+         r2min *= r2min;
